<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="50836" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EPSY/203/50836.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="EPSY" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EPSY.xml">Educational Psychology</subject><course id="203" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EPSY/203.xml">Social Issues Group Dialogues</course></parents><sectionNumber>AD6</sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Exploring Size and Sizeism: This course explores body size and weight-based oppression as a social justice issue alongside other systems of oppression. Topics include socio-historical constructions of size, fatness, and bodies, activism and advocacy around fatness and body positivity, and contemporary case studies in fat studies.  Meets 24-Mar-25 – 12-May-25.  1 Hour (letter-graded) credit, second-half session class. Offered in collaboration with Diversity &amp; Social Justice Education (DSJE). For questions, email dsje@illinois.edu</sectionText><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-03-17Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LBD">Laboratory-Discussion</type><start>03:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>236</roomNumber><buildingName>Wohlers Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Blanden" firstName="K">Blanden, K</instructor><instructor lastName="Fitzjarrald" firstName="A">Fitzjarrald, A</instructor><instructor lastName="Threadgill" firstName="R">Threadgill, R</instructor></instructors><